Merger Agreement: Article 4.7 Enhanced Proposal Assessment.

(a) The Board shall determine whether a proposal qualifies as an Enhanced Offer only after a comprehensive evaluation of the following criteria:
    (i) Financial Metrics: Detailed quantitative analysis provided by the Senior Financial Advisor;
    (ii) Strategic Alignment: Assessment of the proposal’s fit with the company’s long-term strategic objectives;
    (iii) Regulatory Impact: Evaluation of potential legal and compliance issues as indicated by the Compliance Committee;
    (iv) Risk Management: Identification and analysis of potential risks by the Risk Oversight Team.

(b) Notwithstanding any favorable financial data in subsection (a)(i), the Enhanced Offer shall be declared superior only if the Board confirms that satisfactory consideration has been given to criteria (ii), (iii), and (iv) as well.

Question: Is "financial point of view" the sole consideration when determining whether an Enhanced Offer is superior?
