Merger Agreement: SECTION 8.7. Modified Tender Offers. <omitted> 
(a) In evaluating any Tender Proposal, the Board shall consider not only the financial attributes of the offer (including valuation metrics and liquidity analysis) but also a spectrum of non-financial factors, such as market volatility, competitive positioning, and strategic insights from independent legal and industry advisors; 
(b) The Board is further required to convene with a panel of external consultants to deliberate on the potential long-term operational synergies and fiduciary implications of the offer, thereby integrating both quantitative and qualitative assessments; 
(c) Consequently, the determination of a Superior Offer does not rest solely on financial metrics but is contingent on a holistic review that weighs both financial and non-financial elements to fulfill its broader fiduciary responsibilities.

